# Build context for every Containerfile in this repo is the repository root, and the root holds a
# `target/` directory that reaches tens of gigabytes on a developer machine. Without this file that
# whole tree is sent to the builder before the first instruction runs.
#
# Allow-list, not a block-list: everything is excluded, then the three paths the Containerfiles
# actually COPY are added back. A block-list silently starts shipping whatever directory lands at
# the root next; this way the context can only grow when someone edits this file on purpose.
#
# Adding a `COPY <path>` to a Containerfile therefore means adding `!<path>` here, or the build
# fails with "<path>: not found".
*

# The workspace manifest and its lockfile. `--locked` in the build makes the lockfile load-bearing:
# omitting it turns every image build into a dependency re-resolution.
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock

# Both workspace member roots. Neither is optional for either image: `members = ["bins/*",
# "crates/*"]` means cargo loads every member manifest before it can build any single package, so
# an image that compiles only `preauth-proxy` still needs `crates/` on disk to parse the workspace.
!bins
!crates

# Re-excluded after the two lines above, because `!bins`/`!crates` pull in their whole subtree.
# Nothing here produces a per-member `target/` today (the workspace shares the root one), but a
# stray `cargo build` run from inside a member directory would create one.
bins/**/target
crates/**/target
